# Dependencies & build output
# No trailing slash on purpose: a trailing slash matches DIRECTORIES ONLY, and
# git treats a symlink as a file. The worktree setup recipe makes
# server/web/shared node_modules SYMLINKS to the main checkout, so `node_modules/`
# left them un-ignored and a routine `git add -A` staged them (Cebab-u2a).
# `node_modules` (no slash) matches a dir OR a symlink of that name at any depth.
node_modules
dist/
*.tsbuildinfo

# Logs
*.log
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*

# Local env files (.env.example is committed)
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Editor / OS
.DS_Store
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo

# Local cebab data — kept out of git on purpose
data/
logs/
*.sqlite
*.sqlite-journal
*.sqlite-wal
*.sqlite-shm

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The workshop, not the tool.
#
# Cebab is what this repo ships. The autonomous development loop that builds
# it, the Beads issue graph, the live-quota Playground smokes and the agent
# briefing are one developer's local apparatus: none of it is needed to build,
# test or run Cebab, and a public repo carrying it invites the reader to
# mistake the workshop for the product.
#
# THE COST, STATED SO IT IS NOT REDISCOVERED. The loop's own ~7k lines of
# tests no longer run in CI, because `npm test` cannot collect what git does
# not carry. That is the same mistake `scripts/kanban-sync.mjs` made — it was
# gitignored and CI therefore never ran its 20 tests (Cebab-8fa). The
# difference is that this one is deliberate and paid for: the loop's gate runs
# its own suite explicitly before it may publish anything. If that step is
# ever dropped, this apparatus is unverified.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Loop runtime state — ledger, HALT kill switch, console tee, resolved config.
.loop/

# Loop code, its rehearsal harness and its revert-check.
/scripts/loop.mjs
/scripts/loop.test.mjs
/scripts/loop-rehearsal.mjs
/scripts/loop-rehearsal.test.mjs
/scripts/revert-check.mjs
/scripts/revertCheck.test.mjs
/scripts/lib/loop/

# Loop documentation — specs for the driver and for the change it must produce.
/docs/AUTONOMOUS_LOOP_SPEC.md
/docs/LOOP_DEVELOPMENT_STANDARD.md

# The agent briefing and the contributor guide. The product claims CLAUDE.md
# used to carry moved to docs/safety-and-security.md + SECURITY.md first (#508)
# so nothing public depends on either file.
/CLAUDE.md
/CONTRIBUTING.md

# Claude Code's own per-checkout state. `.claude/scheduled_tasks.lock` was
# TRACKED until this commit and held a live session id, pid and boot timestamp
# from one machine; `.git/info/exclude` silenced the rest, which no clone
# inherits.
.claude/

# Cebab's own per-checkout state, when the tool is pointed at this repo — and
# the second half of the same finding. `.claude/` was moved here from
# `.git/info/exclude` above; `.cebab/` was left behind in it, so the sentence
# directly above stayed true of this directory for another three weeks. It
# holds operator- and agent-authored review notes (three markdown files here
# today), and any clone running Cebab on itself was one `git add -A` from
# publishing them.
.cebab/


# `npm run coverage` output. The run is a measurement, not a gate, so the
# report is regenerated on demand and never committed — a stale one would be
# read as current, which is the whole failure mode `vitest.config.ts`'s
# coverage block was added to stop.
/coverage/

# npm/yarn output
*.tgz
.npm/

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Local issue-tracking setup — Beads + Kanban Pro. Deliberately NOT in git.
#
# This is one developer's local workflow, not part of the project: the issue
# graph lives in an embedded Dolt DB under .beads/ and is mirrored to a Kanban
# Pro board outside the repo (~/Kanban/Cebab). None of it is needed to build,
# test or run Cebab, and committing it would push one person's task list onto
# everyone who clones.
#
# Note `bd init` also repoints `core.hooksPath` at .beads/hooks (a local git
# config, so nothing to ignore here). It copies .husky/pre-commit rather than
# replacing it, so lint-staged + gitleaks still run. `npm run setup` re-runs
# husky and points hooks back at .husky/_ if you want beads' hooks gone.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Beads / Dolt
.beads/
.dolt/
*.db
.beads-credential-key
.agents/skills/beads/
.codex/config.toml
.codex/hooks.json
AGENTS.md

# Kanban Pro mirror — the sync script, its test, the workflow doc and the
# slash commands / SessionEnd hook that drive it.
scripts/kanban-sync.mjs
scripts/kanban-sync.test.mjs
docs/BEADS_KANBAN_WORKFLOW.md
.claude/commands/plan-feature.md
.claude/commands/sync-board.md
.claude/hooks/kanban-sync-on-end.sh
.claude/settings.json.bak-before-kanban
_to_delete/
